Stage 3: campaign mission-marker INNER-RING gray (c622/11ba) + be47 blink-phase + f338 cursor colour.

Three asm-verified fixes that take the campaign MISSION-SELECT screen (f338) to AE=0 vs the genuine
DOSBox capture (from 114/142 residual): the inner marker ring gray, the inverted selected-marker blink,
and the wrong mouse-cursor colour on the whole screen (patch 149's far-call dummy 0xf69 set al=0x69=105).

The campaign MISSION-SELECT screen (f338) rendered its 4 mission marker boxes 99.8% bit-exact; the
residual was the marker INNER ring (drawn index-0 black by the port, dark-gray index-2 by DOSBox) plus
an inverted selected-marker blink.  Both are asm-verified reconstruction bugs, not palette/timing fudges.

ROOT CAUSE 1 -- the inner ring is ALWAYS color index 2 (gray), by the 11ba asm itself.
  be47 draws each marker as three nested box outlines: [0x61e]=119f (inset-1, caller's al = state colour),
  [0x61a]=11db (outer, al=0 black), [0x622]=11ba (inset-2).  The asm of 11ba (re_out/fist_mga_image.bin
  0x11ba) is:
      11ba: b8 02 00     mov ax,0x2          ; AX=2  -> AL=2 !!
      11bd: 01 07        add [bx],ax          ; shrink rect by 2 (uses AX)
      ...  (sub [bx+4],ax etc.)
      11c9: e8 0f 00     call 0x11db          ; 11db draws with AL -- which is now 2, NOT the caller's al
  i.e. 11ba reuses the inset amount (2) as the fill colour: `mov ax,2` clobbers AL to 2 before the
  box-outline draw, so the innermost ring is UNCONDITIONALLY drawn palette index 2 (the dark-gray bevel
  highlight).  Contrast 119f (inset-1) which uses `inc [bx]`/`dec [bx+4]` -- it never touches AX, so it
  preserves the caller's al -- and 11db which push/pop's ax around the clip call.  Only 11ba clobbers al.
  Patch 138 reconstructed 11ba as `FUN_0000_11db(bx, al)` (passing the caller's al through), which is
  wrong: the real 11ba passes AL=2.  Fix: call 11db with the literal 2.  (11ba is reached ONLY via be47's
  c622 -- verified: c622 has no other caller -- so this touches only the campaign markers; the SELECT
  PLAYER title bar that first exercised patch 138 uses 11db/119f only, never 11ba.  Zero regression.)

ROOT CAUSE 2 -- the selected-marker blink was inverted.  be47 asm 0x1be64:
      cmp cx,[0x6db6]                  ; cx == selected mission index?
      jne 1be74                        ; no -> colour by state
      mov al,0                         ; yes: al=0 (black)
      test [0x452],0x10
      je  1be8a                        ; if (frame-timer bit4 CLEAR) -> draw with al=0 (black)
      ; else fall through to 1be74 (colour by state)
  So the SELECTED marker's inset-1 ring is BLACK when [0x452]&0x10 == 0 and the STATE colour when set --
  patch 149 had the condition as `(tick & 0x10) != 0 -> al=0`, the opposite phase.  Fix the test.

Both fixes are needed to reach AE=0 vs the genuine DOSBox capture (which shows the inner ring gray and,
at its capture phase, the selected marker black).  The flow pins the capture tick-phase deterministically
via FIST_DUMPTICK (see tools/verify.sh campaign-missions) so native == wasm == DOSBox.

